feat(server,db): unify memory notes into the notes facet + 0052 migration (#620)

Add the fail-loud 0052 data migration that copies every memory_notes row into
the unified notes facet (kind='note') under the same entry_id, flips the entry
type memory_note->note, repoints the memory_prompts FK to notes, and drops the
memory_notes table. Schema drops the memory_notes table and the memory_note
entry type, repointing memoryPrompts.noteEntryId to notes.

Introduce the Notes-owned boundary primitives insertNoteInTx / deleteNoteInTx
and getNoteById, and refactor Reader create/delete, Memory writeMemory /
editMemoryNote / deleteMemoryNote, all Memory reads, and the Timeline to source
the note body/capture-source/provenance from the one notes store. Memory notes
are the unanchored kind='note' rows, so reader notes never leak into a Memory
surface; the Timeline folds the memory-note projection into the single note row
carrying capture source + prompt count.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
